{"agent":"bgm","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The regression never runs `research add`. Both `run_cli` calls are `research --question ...` with no `add` subcommand, so a failure or pass here does not lock bug Ba3d7e2ecfe. Given a CLI where `ddflow research add --question …` is the filing command and bare `research` is another mode, this test can stay green while `research add` still prints `shares:` and omits a trailing `research <id> recorded (CONFIRMED)` line.","digest":"676e0c623b7d6954","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_research_add_output.py:25","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_research_add_output.py:25"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The test demands the duplicate list on stderr (`\"It reads like\" in err and \"shares:\" in err`) before it checks the confirmation. The bug is that `shares:` is printed before the confirmation and buries the id; a correct fix can leave that list on stdout and only make the last stdout line `research <id> recorded (CONFIRMED)`. That input fails this test. The reverse also holds: if the list is not on stderr, the assertion dies before `out.rstrip().endswith(...)` and the regex, so the test does not fail for the promised reason.","digest":"d9f0bebd5e1cf894","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_research_add_output.py:47","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_research_add_output.py:47"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":1921,"diff_sha":"5019be082c125a014db6b76280bd1a34bab1ce84814ff3fc4df1d60bbd6cfbc3","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-Ba3d7e2ecfe","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":35.5,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"bd27972e4625c906","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Ba3d7e2ecfe.rubbe